# The random-search tuner, run independently on two different laws (the control and #25), drove the diagonal discount from 0.916 down to ~0.70-0.76, below two orthogonal steps (0.884), so it keeps saying the same thing: value should not travel diagonally. Read as structure, that is a Manhattan wave: value spreads only through the four orthogonal neighbours, so the field takes the grid's own geometry (walls, doorways, corridors are axis-aligned), corner-cutting through a wall's diagonal gap gets no value, and the agent's diagonal steps are only those two straight steps would justify. On the best-train law (#10, the sweep), with the max8 term removed.

channel source
channel solid
channel free
channel thing
channel scent
channel here
channel value
channel unknown
channel vast
channel confinement
channel dwell
channel frust
channel trail
channel been
channel injection

rule unknown:
  when 1
  set unknown = (0.8696 - free) * (1 - solid)

rule vast:
  when 1
  set vast = 0.3 * unknown + 0.8306 * avg8(vast)

rule confine:
  when 1
  set confinement = sum8(solid)

rule dwell:
  when 1
  set dwell = where(here > 0, min(1, dwell + 0.005203), 0.7418 * dwell)

rule frust:
  when 1
  set frust = max(here * dwell, 0.95 * max8(frust))

# the path walked, slowly fading; scrolls with the map
rule trail:
  when 1
  set trail = max(here, 0.998 * trail)

# a wide blur of the path: how much of the agent's own past lies around a cell
rule been:
  when 1
  set been = 0.2 * trail + 0.8 * avg8(been)

# frontier on the side the agent came from counts less: the sweep goes on away from its past
rule inject:
  when 1
  set injection = max(max(thing, source * where(thing + scent > 0, 1.358, (0.4275 + 1.5 * vast) * (1 - min(1, 3 * been)))) / (1 + 0.4454 * confinement), frust * solid * max8(free) * leak)

# a MANHATTAN wave: value travels only orthogonally, so a diagonal neighbour is worth what two
# straight steps are; the plan is in the grid's own geometry (walls and doors are axis-aligned)
rule wave:
  when 1
  set value = max(injection, 0.94 * max4(value) * (0.85 + 0.15 * min(1, free))) * (1 - solid * (1.028 - leak))
